  "summary": "Steering gear box mounting to the frame, the flexible coupling (rag joint) flange between the steering column and the gear, and the steering wheel, hub and horn cover at the top of the column. The gear bolts to the frame with bolts, lock washers and nuts; the coupling is held by a pinch bolt and nuts with lock washers; the wheel is screwed to the hub with three screws and held on the shaft by the nut and washer that come with the column. Related sheets: horn cam & spring in UPC 12.",
